                <h2>Achieve Clearer, Healthier Skin</h2>
                <p>Acne is the most common skin condition in the United States, affecting people of all ages. Whether you're a teenager dealing with breakouts or an adult experiencing hormonal acne, our dermatologists can help you achieve clearer, healthier skin.</p>
                
                <h3>Types of Acne We Treat</h3>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Comedonal Acne:</strong> Blackheads and whiteheads caused by clogged pores</li>
                    <li><strong>Inflammatory Acne:</strong> Red, swollen pimples and pustules</li>
                    <li><strong>Cystic Acne:</strong> Deep, painful cysts that can cause scarring</li>
                    <li><strong>Hormonal Acne:</strong> Breakouts related to hormonal fluctuations</li>
                    <li><strong>Adult Acne:</strong> Acne persisting or developing in adulthood</li>
                </ul>
                
                <h3>Our Acne Treatment Options</h3>
                <p>We develop personalized treatment plans based on your acne type, severity, and skin type:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li><strong>Topical Medications:</strong> Prescription retinoids, benzoyl peroxide, and antibiotics</li>
                    <li><strong>Oral Medications:</strong> Antibiotics, hormonal treatments, and isotretinoin (Accutane) for severe cases</li>
                    <li><strong>Chemical Peels:</strong> Medical-grade peels to unclog pores and reduce breakouts</li>
                    <li><strong>Extraction:</strong> Professional removal of comedones</li>
                    <li><strong>Light & Laser Therapy:</strong> Targeted treatments to kill bacteria and reduce inflammation</li>
                </ul>
                
                <h3>Acne Scar Treatment</h3>
                <p>If acne has left scars, we offer treatments to improve skin texture:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li>Microneedling to stimulate collagen</li>
                    <li>Chemical peels for surface irregularities</li>
                    <li>Laser resurfacing for more significant scarring</li>
                </ul>
                
                <h3>What to Expect</h3>
                <p>During your acne consultation, we will:</p>
                <ul>
                    <li>Evaluate your skin and acne type</li>
                    <li>Discuss your skincare routine and lifestyle factors</li>
                    <li>Create a customized treatment plan</li>
                    <li>Provide education on preventing future breakouts</li>
                    <li>Schedule follow-ups to monitor progress and adjust treatment</li>
                </ul>
