<section class="faq-section">
    <div class="container">
        <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
        
        <div class="faq-item">
            <h3>What causes acne?</h3>
            <p>Acne occurs when hair follicles become clogged with oil and dead skin cells. Contributing factors include hormones, genetics, bacteria, certain medications, and diet. Our dermatologists can help identify your specific triggers.</p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="faq-item">
            <h3>Can adults get acne?</h3>
            <p>Yes, adult acne is very common, especially in women. Hormonal changes, stress, certain medications, and skincare products can all contribute to adult acne. We offer treatments specifically designed for adult skin.</p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="faq-item">
            <h3>How long does acne treatment take to work?</h3>
            <p>Most acne treatments take 6-8 weeks to show significant improvement. It's important to be patient and consistent with your treatment plan. We'll monitor your progress and adjust as needed.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
